From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:58:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] wifi: ath12k: set the QMI chunk size limit for the
 WCN7860

Commit 4e286c780d75 ("wifi: ath12k: use per-device max QMI chunk size")
replaced the fixed 2 MB limit in ath12k_qmi_alloc_chunk() with
hw_params->qmi_max_chunk_size, and set it for each device it knew of.
The WCN7860 entry was added out of tree before that field existed and
was carried over without it, so the limit is 0 there: every failed DMA
allocation of a target memory chunk, even a small one on the retry,
then asks the firmware to retry again ("will try later with small
size") instead of failing with -ENOMEM.

The WCN7860 uses the WCN7850's WLFW service and the same HMT firmware
family, which retries with 512 KB chunks; use SZ_512K as the WCN7850
entry does.

Not measured on the WCN7860: the allocation does not fail on the
OnePlus Pad 4 in normal use, so this only changes the error path.

Fixes: 4e286c780d75 ("wifi: ath12k: use per-device max QMI chunk size")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
index d3bedc3dd..b1578f4ec 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -738,6 +738,7 @@ static const struct ath12k_hw_params ath12k_wifi7_hw_params[] = {
 		.max_radios = 2,
 		.single_pdev_only = true,
 		.qmi_service_ins_id = ATH12K_QMI_WLFW_SERVICE_INS_ID_V01_WCN7850,
+		.qmi_max_chunk_size = SZ_512K,
 		.internal_sleep_clock = true,
 
 		.hw_ops = &qcc2072_ops,
-- 
